Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-16-2001||08:54 PM||||What the heck is bump steer?  And whats the correction kit??<P>I was looking on ebay and came across a bumpsteer correction kit for the 84-87s.  Just curious to what it does and if its an aftermarket thing, or were the cars equipped and this a replacement???<P>Any info as always aprreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Zoom88||10-16-2001||09:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>What the heck is bump steer?  And whats the correction kit??<P>I was looking on ebay and came across a bumpsteer correction kit for the 84-87s.  Just curious to what it does and if its an aftermarket thing, or were the cars equipped and this a replacement???<P>Any info as always aprreciated.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>What the heck is bump steer?  And whats the correction kit??<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><FONT COLOR="blue">The kit consist basically of special outer tie-rod ends and are primarily designed for racing. I believe Bump Steer is refering to the shift or jerking of the front suspension caused by bumps or irregularities in the pavement</FONT>||||reg||1
